<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joan II of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1312">1312</a>–<a href="/years/1349">1349</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joan II was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1328, the daughter of Louis X of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Excluded from the French throne after her father's death, she was recognised in Navarre when the direct Capetian line ended, and ruled jointly with her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-of-navarre">Philip of Évreux</a>. Their son Charles II, called the Bad, succeeded her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-ii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Joan II of Navarre" width="236" height="303" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Acoma · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jana2Navarra_SaintDenis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
